Swap the DNT default for the GPC default

Chromium 152 ships complete GPC machinery and the shared Helium patch
already wires the kHeliumGlobalPrivacyControl pref through renderer
preferences, workers, and navigator.globalPrivacyControl, registering it
with default false. The DNT default currently ships as true because the
vendored Vanadium 0122 patch flips the shared registration from false to
true, and neither existing patch may change: editing Vanadium 0122 breaks
the vendored-patch no-modify rule, and editing the shared patch's GPC
default would break Vanadium 0122's zero-fuzz application because its
hunk context includes the GPC registration line. Both defaults are
therefore flipped here, by layering, in one minimal hunk that replaces
the two registration default arguments (duplicate RegisterBooleanPref
calls for the same path DCHECK-fail, so re-registration cannot override
an earlier default). The SYNCABLE_PREF flag on the DNT registration is
preserved. Result: no DNT header, Sec-GPC: 1 on document, worker, and
browser-initiated requests, navigator.doNotTrack === null, and
navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true. Users keep the settings
toggles; the GPC/DNT settings strings already exist.
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
@@ -173,9 +173,9 @@
   registry->RegisterDictionaryPref(prefs::kBrowserWindowPlacementPopup);
   registry->RegisterDictionaryPref(prefs::kAppWindowPlacement);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      prefs::kEnableDoNotTrack, true,
+      prefs::kEnableDoNotTrack, false,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
-  registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumGlobalPrivacyControl, false);
+  registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumGlobalPrivacyControl, true);
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kPrintPreviewUseSystemDefaultPrinter,
                                 false);
